<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21775" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γελᾰσ-ῖνος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>laugher</i>, of Democritus, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				4.20
			</span></i>: fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γελασίνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ γ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδόντες</span>) <i>the grinners</i>, i. e. <i>the front
				teeth</i>, which show when one laughs, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.91
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> mostly pl.,
				<i>dimples</i>, which appear in the cheeks when persons laugh, <i><span class="en">
				Mart.
				7.25
			</span></i> (sg.), <i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				2.188
			</span></i>; also of <i>dimples in the hinder parts</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				1.39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				5.34
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Rufin.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
